---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/common/Breadcrumbs.astro';

const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy Policy' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  seo={{
    title: 'Privacy Policy | Easy Utility India',
    description: 'Learn how Easy Utility India protects your data. All document processing happens strictly inside your local web browser with zero server storage.',
  }}
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10 sm:py-16">
    <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />

    <article class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-6 sm:p-10 shadow-sm prose prose-slate max-w-none text-slate-700 space-y-6">
      <div>
        <span class="text-xs font-bold px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-700 border border-emerald-200 uppercase tracking-wider inline-block mb-3">
          Privacy Guarantee
        </span>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 tracking-tight">
          Privacy Policy
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-2">Last updated: November 1, 2026</p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-emerald-50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-emerald-200 text-xs text-emerald-900 leading-relaxed font-medium">
        <strong>Executive Summary:</strong> When you use Easy Utility India to compress images, merge PDFs, or split documents, your files are never uploaded to any server. All processing runs 100% inside your web browser on your phone or computer.
      </div>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">1. Information We Do NOT Collect</h2>
        <p>
          Unlike conventional utility platforms, Easy Utility India does not operate server-side file processors. When you interact with our file utilities (Image to PDF, Merge PDF, Split PDF, PDF Preview, Image Resizer, Image Compressor, JPG to PNG Converter):
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li>We do <strong>not</strong> upload your documents or images to our servers.</li>
          <li>We do <strong>not</strong> store your personal files on cloud buckets or storage databases.</li>
          <li>We do <strong>not</strong> read, inspect, or sell the contents of your documents or calculation inputs.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">2. Technical Processing Model</h2>
        <p>
          Our tools operate via client-side JavaScript APIs (HTML5 Canvas, File API, and WebAssembly). All memory manipulation happens within the sandbox of your own device's web browser. When you refresh or close your browser tab, all memory allocated for your documents is immediately discarded by your device operating system.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">3. Cookies, Web Storage, and Hosting Logs</h2>
        <p>
          Easy Utility India does not install invasive tracking cookies or create behavioral profiles. We treat your privacy with highest standard:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li><strong>Client Memory (RAM):</strong> When you open a tool, document data is stored only in temporary memory (JavaScript variables) while your browser tab remains open. No files or images are written to persistent server databases.</li>
          <li><strong>Local Browser Storage:</strong> Tools may store temporary UI state (such as your chosen zoom level or calculator tab) strictly within your device's browser localStorage. This data never leaves your device.</li>
          <li><strong>Infrastructure Logs (Vercel):</strong> Our website is hosted on Vercel's global CDN. Like virtually all web servers, Vercel may log basic HTTP request metadata (such as IP address, user-agent header, requested asset path, and timestamp) solely for network routing, security, and DDoS protection.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">4. Third-Party Advertising & Google AdSense Disclosures</h2>
        <p>
          To maintain all utilities free of charge for Indian students and applicants without paywalls or subscriptions, Easy Utility India is designed to support third-party advertising partners such as Google AdSense.
        </p>
        <p>
          When active, Google and its advertising partners use cookies (such as the DoubleClick cookie) to serve ads to users based on prior visits to this website or other websites on the Internet:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li>Third-party vendors, including Google, use cookies to serve ads based on a user's prior visits to your website or other websites.</li>
          <li>Google's use of advertising cookies enables it and its partners to serve ads based on your visit to our sites and/or other sites on the Internet.</li>
          <li>Users may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-600 underline">Google Ads Settings</a>. Alternatively, users can opt out of a third-party vendor's use of cookies for personalized advertising by visiting <a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-600 underline">aboutads.info</a>.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">5. Contact Regarding Privacy Queries</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions, clarifications, or feedback concerning this Privacy Policy, please open a discussion or issue on our official <a href="https://github.com/patelabhishek55555-source/easy-utility-india/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-brand-600 underline">GitHub Project Tracker</a> or reach out through our <a href="/contact" class="text-brand-600 underline">Contact Page</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
